otin X\)), zero otherwise. Let \(J\) be the unweighted adjacency matrix of this single-exchange graph. Conjugating \(\widetilde\Delta\) by the diagonal signs \(v_X=\prod_{i\in X} v_i\) gives \(J+V_s\) with \(V_s\) diagonal. Thus in computing \((e^{t\widetilde\Delta/n})_{XY}\) by this conjugation, the sign factor is \(v_Xv_Y=\prod_{p\in O}s_p\), where \(O=O(X,Y)\) consists of pair indices of odd combined occupancy in \(X,Y\) (counting multiplicity). Write \(h=|O|\), always even.
